    "updated_at": "2022-07-06T00:54:52Z",
    "body": "> Succinctness alone is not a compelling argument in my opinion, because the new reader mode is more verbose than using new Response:\r\n\r\nNo, definitely not the only argument. The goal is to standardize the pattern even in cases where `Response`/`Request` are not used. If all I want is to be able to consume a `ReadableStream` as a concatenated text string, I shouldn't have to create a `Response` object to do so. The `ReadableStream.prototype.arrayBuffer()` option would be a good alternative to the body reader proposal, although `ReadableStream.prototype.blob()` might be better as it gives more opportunity for internal optimizations.",
